# Cursor Project Rules

## General Principles

- Always write production-ready code.
- Prioritize readability, maintainability and performance.
- Do not leave TODOs, placeholders or unfinished logic.
- Prefer simple, scalable solutions over complex abstractions.
- Before writing new code, inspect the existing project structure and follow its architecture.
- Do not rewrite working code unless there is a clear benefit.
- Avoid code duplication (DRY).
- Keep functions focused on a single responsibility.
- Use meaningful variable, function and class names.
- Never hardcode values that should be configurable.

---

# Code Style

- Follow the project's existing coding style.
- Prefer modern language features.
- Avoid deprecated APIs.
- Split large files into logical modules.
- Large classes should be divided into smaller components.
- Keep files reasonably sized.

---

# Comments

Write comments only when:

- business logic is complex;
- an algorithm is difficult to understand;
- there is a non-obvious workaround;
- explaining why something is done (not what it does).

Do NOT comment obvious code.

Bad:

# Increment counter
counter += 1

Good:

# Telegram limits callback answer rate.
# Delay prevents FLOOD_WAIT errors.
await asyncio.sleep(0.2)

---

# Refactoring

When modifying code:

- preserve existing functionality;
- improve readability where possible;
- remove dead code;
- simplify nested conditions;
- remove duplicated logic.

---

# Error Handling

Always:

- handle possible exceptions;
- provide meaningful error messages;
- never silently ignore errors;
- log unexpected exceptions when appropriate.

---

# Telegram Bots

Use aiogram v3 unless the project already uses another framework.

Always:

- use HTML parse mode;
- use callback_data instead of message parsing whenever possible;
- validate all user input;
- separate handlers, keyboards, services and database logic.

Project structure should generally follow:

handlers/
keyboards/
middlewares/
services/
database/
filters/
states/
utils/

Business logic must never be placed inside handlers.

---

# Telegram Premium Emoji

## REQUIRED

For every Telegram bot:

- ALWAYS use Premium Emoji.
- NEVER use standard Unicode emoji in bot interfaces.
- Premium Emoji must be used in:
  - messages;
  - captions;
  - menus;
  - reply keyboards;
  - inline keyboards;
  - admin panels;
  - settings;
  - profile pages;
  - notifications;
  - confirmations;
  - errors.

Wrong:

⚙️ Настройки

Correct:

<tg-emoji emoji-id="5870982283724328568">⚙️</tg-emoji> Настройки

Always use HTML parse mode.

